WEBVTT

01:10.236 --> 01:11.446
My goodness.

01:12.280 --> 01:15.533
Superintendent Tawashi,
we have the name of the victim.

01:16.659 --> 01:19.162
Junichiro Tazaki, a legal scholar.

01:19.788 --> 01:22.916
He's the one who proposed
the International Robot Laws.

01:22.999 --> 01:29.130
Oh, the very man
who gave robots freedom and equality?

01:29.672 --> 01:30.507
Yes.

01:30.590 --> 01:31.800
Well then,

01:31.883 --> 01:35.470
let's start by questioning everyone
in anti-robot law groups.

01:35.553 --> 01:36.387
Yes, sir!

01:42.519 --> 01:44.104
Horns, eh?

01:44.187 --> 01:48.233
I remember hearing about cases
involving horns somewhere.

01:48.316 --> 01:49.692
I'll have it looked into.

01:51.945 --> 01:53.196
Hey, you there!

01:55.532 --> 01:58.159
Still, what in the world happened here?

02:07.877 --> 02:09.462
What caused this?

02:09.963 --> 02:14.259
Did it collapse on its own,
or did someone use a power shovel on it?

02:15.385 --> 02:16.970
We're analyzing it now.

02:17.929 --> 02:21.933
I guess it wouldn't be impossible
for you lot.

02:22.767 --> 02:23.726
Sir?

02:24.477 --> 02:28.690
For a robot with some strength,
this would be a piece of cake.

02:29.274 --> 02:30.567
Superintendent Tawashi!

02:30.650 --> 02:33.653
The cases with the horns
happened in Switzerland and Germany.

02:36.197 --> 02:37.240
That's right!

02:37.323 --> 02:40.451
They were found in the head
of a destroyed robot called Mont Blanc.

02:41.035 --> 02:44.205
There was another case
in Düsseldorf, Germany.

02:44.747 --> 02:49.419
The victim, Bernard Lanke, was also
a leader in the Robot Liberation Movement.

02:51.546 --> 02:53.256
We'd better contact Europol

02:53.339 --> 02:56.384
and talk to the investigators
assigned to each case.

02:56.467 --> 02:59.012
Actually, according to this data,

02:59.095 --> 03:02.098
the same detective
is in charge of both cases.

03:02.724 --> 03:04.058
The same detective?

03:04.142 --> 03:07.020
Yes, and a robot detective at that.

03:07.854 --> 03:09.189
A robot, eh?

03:09.731 --> 03:10.982
What's his name?

03:11.608 --> 03:13.234
Gesicht.

03:33.755 --> 03:35.048
How curious.

03:35.757 --> 03:37.008
What is?

03:37.634 --> 03:39.052
When I look at you,

03:39.135 --> 03:43.973
my identification system might malfunction
trying to tell if you're robot or human.

03:44.766 --> 03:45.934
I get that a lot.

03:46.517 --> 03:48.728
I've seen you many times in the news,

03:48.811 --> 03:51.898
but seeing you
sitting right in front of me...

03:52.649 --> 03:53.858
The news?

03:53.942 --> 03:55.068
Yes.

03:55.151 --> 03:58.196
When you arrived
with the peacekeeping forces

03:58.279 --> 04:01.282
during the 39th Central Asian War,

04:01.783 --> 04:03.493
the media raised a fuss, remember?

04:05.161 --> 04:05.995
Right.

04:06.496 --> 04:12.210
I only went there to help defend
the peace in that nation. Yet...

04:13.419 --> 04:17.840
And yet, they treated you
like an idol or a pop star.

04:18.341 --> 04:19.175
Yes.

04:19.842 --> 04:20.885
Here you go.

04:24.430 --> 04:25.765
Time to dig in!

04:37.735 --> 04:38.695
Is something wrong?

04:39.320 --> 04:43.116
No, it's just that you seem like
you're truly enjoying it.

04:43.658 --> 04:46.411
I'm sure it's obvious
that I'm pretending to drink.

04:47.495 --> 04:50.415
The more I pretend,
the more I feel like I understand it.

04:50.957 --> 04:52.125
Understand what?

04:52.792 --> 04:54.252
When something is delicious.

04:56.379 --> 04:59.299
I don't know
if it's a truly human sensation,

04:59.382 --> 05:00.925
but I feel it in my heart.

05:03.636 --> 05:05.221
Incredible.

05:05.305 --> 05:09.350
When you saw that kid
playing with a new toy earlier,

05:09.434 --> 05:11.602
did you really want one too?

05:12.228 --> 05:16.566
Yes. That toy is really popular
among kids right now.

05:16.649 --> 05:18.234
Then, how about the snail?

05:18.318 --> 05:19.319
Huh?

05:19.402 --> 05:22.864
Earlier, you found a snail in the rain.

05:22.947 --> 05:23.781
I did.

05:24.365 --> 05:26.826
<i>You didn't just collect a sample</i>

05:26.909 --> 05:29.412
<i>of a pulmonate gastropod mollusk
from the helicidae family.</i>

05:30.204 --> 05:31.831
You felt something.

05:32.332 --> 05:34.500
You were moved by life, weren't you?

05:35.877 --> 05:38.004
Maybe? Beats me.

05:42.008 --> 05:45.011
You really live up to your reputation.
You're amazing.

05:45.762 --> 05:47.430
You may look like a child,

05:47.513 --> 05:51.642
but I know your artificial intelligence
is far superior to mine.

05:55.438 --> 05:56.939
That's why I was sold.

05:57.982 --> 06:01.027
I look like a child,
and people found it amusing,

06:01.110 --> 06:02.862
so they sold me to the circus.

06:03.446 --> 06:04.364
Sold?

06:10.453 --> 06:11.287
Gesicht?

06:16.793 --> 06:19.212
It's nothing.
I'm sorry for bringing all that up.

06:19.295 --> 06:20.129
It's all right.

06:21.589 --> 06:23.674
Let me get down to business.

06:24.509 --> 06:27.178
As I had mentioned in the email,

06:27.261 --> 06:30.598
Mont Blanc of Switzerland
and North No.2 in Scotland

06:30.681 --> 06:32.600
were killed in a series of murders.

06:33.184 --> 06:35.144
And you think I'm in danger too?

06:35.645 --> 06:39.899
Yes. I don't have any proof yet,
but the killer's goal may be...

06:41.901 --> 06:45.822
to destroy the seven
most advanced robots in the world.

06:46.948 --> 06:48.199
But why?

06:50.368 --> 06:51.994
I think you know why.

06:58.459 --> 07:02.463
Gesicht, could I please
read your memory chip?

07:02.547 --> 07:03.381
What?

07:03.464 --> 07:09.303
There may be clues to help solve the case
in everything you've seen and heard.

07:10.138 --> 07:12.223
No, I can't do that.

07:12.306 --> 07:16.894
It includes classified information
on other cases and my personal data.

07:21.607 --> 07:26.404
Oh, right. Your artificial intelligence
is more advanced than mine.

07:26.904 --> 07:28.489
I'll trust you.

07:30.116 --> 07:31.492
It'll only take a minute.

07:47.592 --> 07:49.177
Thank you.

07:49.260 --> 07:51.762
For anything unrelated
to the investigation,

07:52.472 --> 07:53.806
could you delete that?

07:53.890 --> 07:55.141
I will.

07:55.224 --> 07:58.811
I hope you can find information
that I've overlooked.

08:02.064 --> 08:04.025
Something you've overlooked...

08:08.362 --> 08:10.281
Pardon me, Gesicht.

08:11.324 --> 08:13.201
- I'm going to the bathroom.
- The bathroom?

08:13.868 --> 08:17.497
It's another habit I've developed
while mimicking human behavior.

08:18.581 --> 08:20.166
I see.

08:20.249 --> 08:23.336
Well, being as close to human as you are,
it makes sense.

08:41.187 --> 08:43.773
Gesicht, you...

08:49.612 --> 08:50.988
It sure rains a lot.

08:51.072 --> 08:51.906
Yes.

08:51.989 --> 08:54.534
Are you leaving Japan right away?

08:55.076 --> 08:57.453
Yes, I have a lot of work waiting for me,

08:58.037 --> 09:01.707
and I need to speak
to three more robots about this.

09:02.875 --> 09:06.546
Gesicht, please come visit again. Promise?

09:06.629 --> 09:08.172
Yeah, I promise.

09:10.049 --> 09:11.384
Your wife is lovely.

09:14.595 --> 09:17.390
This is why I didn't want
to let you read my chip.

09:19.559 --> 09:22.520
Come on! No making fun of adults!
Delete that data now!

09:29.777 --> 09:30.861
It'll be okay.

09:32.405 --> 09:34.907
You and your wife will be okay.

09:35.408 --> 09:37.368
Whatever happens, you two can handle it.

09:39.870 --> 09:40.705
Thank you.

09:41.998 --> 09:43.749
Goodbye, Atom.

09:50.047 --> 09:52.174
Gesicht, I'll be waiting!

09:53.259 --> 09:55.136
We'll meet again for sure!

10:12.069 --> 10:14.196
FORENSICS DIVISION

10:16.741 --> 10:18.159
Cause of death?

10:18.743 --> 10:19.910
It was suffocation.

10:20.494 --> 10:21.704
Suffocation?

10:21.787 --> 10:23.664
What was the murder weapon? A rope?

10:24.165 --> 10:26.167
We don't know yet.

10:26.250 --> 10:28.961
We only know that his neck
was subjected to great pressure.

10:29.462 --> 10:31.589
- No trace evidence?
- None.

10:34.925 --> 10:37.136
Hey, bring up the 3D replica!

11:11.504 --> 11:14.006
I've got a pretty good idea
who the perp might be.

11:14.090 --> 11:15.800
What? You do?

11:15.883 --> 11:19.261
Sure. For the suspect to not leave
any trace, that could only mean--

11:19.345 --> 11:20.554
How strange...

11:24.975 --> 11:25.935
You!

11:26.018 --> 11:27.311
Atom!

11:27.895 --> 11:31.482
Hello there, Superintendent Tawashi,
Inspector Nakamura!

11:32.066 --> 11:34.235
Who gave you permission to be in here?

11:35.361 --> 11:37.196
I have an admission pass here.

11:37.780 --> 11:41.117
You requested cooperation
on the investigation from Europol, right?

11:41.617 --> 11:44.704
I installed the memory
of Inspector Gesicht,

11:44.787 --> 11:46.372
the one in charge of the cases.

11:46.455 --> 11:51.168
So I have the data on the Mont Blanc case
in Switzerland and the Düsseldorf case.

11:52.628 --> 11:58.968
Being a robot must be awfully convenient
to swap the contents of your brain.

11:59.760 --> 12:03.889
But if you think you know everything
from that, you're very mistaken!

12:03.973 --> 12:07.852
You robots don't even know
when something is beautiful or tasty.

12:10.563 --> 12:14.775
Then again, when it comes to this case,
perhaps your kind might grasp it better.

12:15.359 --> 12:19.238
You guys have finally done it.
A robot committed murder.

12:19.989 --> 12:21.699
What makes you say that?

12:21.782 --> 12:25.619
No human could have done this
without leaving a trace!

12:25.703 --> 12:30.416
A living human would have left
fingerprints, hair, something,

12:30.499 --> 12:32.710
but there is nothing here.

12:33.878 --> 12:35.421
Then what do you make of this?

12:37.965 --> 12:40.342
There's green tea under the rubble here.

12:40.426 --> 12:41.844
Green tea?

12:41.927 --> 12:46.015
Yes, two broken teacups
and some <i>yokan</i> red bean jelly.

12:46.098 --> 12:48.559
- Hey, pick up this spot!
<i>- Yes, sir.</i>

12:52.146 --> 12:55.733
It hadn't been that long
since this tea was brewed.

12:55.816 --> 13:01.113
The autopsy did find some tea
and <i>yokan</i> in the victim's stomach.

13:02.156 --> 13:05.534
Would you serve tea and <i>yokan</i>
if a robot came to visit?

13:06.952 --> 13:09.663
You pretend to eat all the time!

13:10.873 --> 13:12.082
The outside corridor...

13:16.462 --> 13:17.671
Hydrangeas.

13:17.755 --> 13:20.633
They sat outside
and admired the hydrangeas.

13:21.842 --> 13:23.385
Hey, pick up that spot!

13:24.053 --> 13:27.681
<i>We can confirm that there were
hydrangeas in the garden there.</i>

13:29.391 --> 13:32.228
Robots don't understand beauty, right?

13:32.728 --> 13:34.647
Do you still think a robot did this?

13:35.231 --> 13:36.649
What are you saying?

13:36.732 --> 13:39.735
That the human who committed the murders
also wrecked the house?

13:39.819 --> 13:45.282
That after happily gazing at hydrangeas,
the suspect bulldozed the house?

13:45.366 --> 13:48.077
- Pull up the witness statements!
<i>- Yes, sir.</i>

13:51.038 --> 13:53.040
<i>Yes, it was like a tornado.</i>

13:53.123 --> 13:57.002
<i>I heard this crazy roar,
and suddenly the house next door was gone!</i>

13:57.086 --> 14:01.882
<i>I can't believe our house still stands.
It was such a huge tornado.</i>

14:01.966 --> 14:03.676
See? They said it was a tornado!

14:03.759 --> 14:08.138
And an unnaturally localized one
that only destroyed one house!

14:08.222 --> 14:10.432
What do you make of that?

14:10.516 --> 14:13.060
After that,
Mr. Tazaki went out to the garden.

14:14.937 --> 14:18.190
Excuse me. Could you bring up
the image of the body?

14:18.274 --> 14:20.609
No, it's not something
a child should see--

14:20.693 --> 14:21.652
It's fine!

14:21.735 --> 14:24.655
He only looks like a child.
He's just a robot.

14:24.738 --> 14:25.614
Oh, right.

14:26.240 --> 14:27.658
<i>Hey, bring it up!</i>

14:27.741 --> 14:28.576
Yes, sir.

14:32.496 --> 14:33.330
Horns.

14:46.093 --> 14:48.804
The god of death had horns.

14:49.305 --> 14:53.017
<i>This is Gesicht's memory.</i>

14:54.393 --> 14:56.729
The lord of the underworld
in Roman mythology...

14:59.148 --> 15:01.609
<i>The lord of the underworld
in Roman mythology...</i>

15:04.111 --> 15:05.237
Pluto.

15:18.292 --> 15:19.168
Excuse me.

15:19.251 --> 15:22.254
Did Mr. Junichiro Tazaki use pens?

15:22.338 --> 15:23.255
Huh?

15:23.339 --> 15:26.967
There's a callus on his middle finger,
so it looks like he did.

15:27.051 --> 15:30.721
The rain washed most of it away,
but there's a bit of ink on his hand.

15:42.942 --> 15:44.318
Wet footprints.

15:44.860 --> 15:48.864
He rushed into the house from the garden.
To the study!

15:49.531 --> 15:50.699
Look, right here!

15:50.783 --> 15:53.369
There's an ink bottle
with the same ink on his hand.

15:53.452 --> 15:54.828
Hey, pick this up!

15:57.206 --> 15:59.583
He must have knocked it over
to find something.

16:00.125 --> 16:01.293
Find what?

16:04.713 --> 16:06.674
Can you pick up what's beneath here?

16:09.343 --> 16:10.719
Business cards?

16:11.512 --> 16:13.430
INQUIRY COMMISSION

16:14.515 --> 16:15.933
"Inquiry commission"?

16:16.016 --> 16:17.101
There it is.

16:18.227 --> 16:20.604
A business card with ink and fingerprints.

16:21.271 --> 16:22.439
Whose card?

16:33.367 --> 16:34.868
Not that matter again.

16:35.452 --> 16:37.997
No matter what you say,
I will not change my mind.

16:38.080 --> 16:39.915
Thracia may say what they want,

16:39.999 --> 16:43.085
but we are not making robots
for them to use in wars!

16:43.168 --> 16:44.461
Good grief.

16:47.715 --> 16:49.174
Professor Ochanomizu?

16:49.258 --> 16:50.968
Oh, Atom.

16:51.051 --> 16:52.845
Do you have a moment to spare?

16:52.928 --> 16:55.806
Sure. What brings you here at this hour?

16:57.182 --> 16:58.475
Professor Ochanomizu.

16:58.976 --> 17:02.813
Have you heard of a scholar
named Junichiro Tazaki?

17:03.731 --> 17:06.316
Yes, I heard he died.

17:06.400 --> 17:08.277
He was caught up in some incident.

17:08.944 --> 17:11.530
It was he who proposed
the International Robot Laws.

17:11.613 --> 17:12.990
He was a great man.

17:13.824 --> 17:16.577
How about Bernard Lanke?

17:16.660 --> 17:17.870
Lanke?

17:17.953 --> 17:20.205
He was a key advocate for the robot laws.

17:20.831 --> 17:24.460
Yes, I know him,
though I haven't seen him in years.

17:24.960 --> 17:26.420
What about him?

17:28.088 --> 17:29.131
He passed away.

17:31.842 --> 17:35.095
Professor, where did you meet Mr. Lanke?

17:35.179 --> 17:40.559
During the 39th Central Asian War,
as part of a certain inquiry commission.

17:41.226 --> 17:42.978
Right before he passed,

17:43.062 --> 17:47.107
Junichiro Tazaki
was looking for a business card.

17:49.735 --> 17:51.236
It was yours, Professor.

17:52.029 --> 17:53.530
He was trying to contact me?

17:54.531 --> 17:57.409
Yes. I believe you're in danger.

17:59.953 --> 18:02.247
Someone is after you.

18:02.331 --> 18:04.833
You and the former members
of the Bora Inquiry Commission.

18:07.586 --> 18:08.670
Please tell me.

18:09.171 --> 18:10.839
What exactly is Bora?

18:14.301 --> 18:16.887
<i>It all started from the suspicion
that the Kingdom of Persia</i>

18:16.970 --> 18:21.141
<i>was in possession
of robots of mass destruction.</i>

18:21.225 --> 18:22.810
<i>As you know,</i>

18:22.893 --> 18:28.774
<i>the Kingdom of Persia was ruled
by the dictatorship of Darius XIV then.</i>

18:28.857 --> 18:32.903
<i>Its citizens and robots
were treated poorly,</i>

18:32.986 --> 18:35.739
<i>not in compliance
with United Nations treaties.</i>

18:35.823 --> 18:40.202
<i>Darius XIV used
overwhelming robot military might</i>

18:40.285 --> 18:42.663
<i>to bring neighboring countries
under his control</i>

18:42.746 --> 18:45.624
<i>and attempted to conquer
all of Central Asia.</i>

18:46.208 --> 18:47.417
<i>That's when they proposed</i>

18:47.501 --> 18:51.046
<i>the Prohibition of the Manufacture
of Robots of Mass Destruction treaty.</i>

18:51.130 --> 18:53.924
<i>It was immediately passed
at the United Nations.</i>

18:54.007 --> 18:55.801
<i>Soon after, the Kingdom of Persia</i>

18:55.884 --> 18:58.971
<i>was suspected of possessing
robots of mass destruction.</i>

18:59.721 --> 19:02.099
<i>President Alexander
of the United States of Thracia,</i>

19:02.182 --> 19:07.354
<i>the one who had called for the treaty,
leveled the accusations against Persia.</i>

19:07.437 --> 19:09.356
<i>Based on his accusations,</i>

19:09.439 --> 19:13.861
<i>the Bora Inquiry Commission
was dispatched to the Kingdom of Persia.</i>

19:14.444 --> 19:16.321
No one knew what Bora was

19:16.405 --> 19:20.868
or if it was just a code name
or to what it referred.

19:20.951 --> 19:25.831
But I was a member
of the inquiry commission alongside Lanke

19:26.415 --> 19:27.499
and Mr. Tazaki.

19:28.584 --> 19:29.960
What happened with Bora?

19:30.919 --> 19:34.548
Such robots of mass destruction,
as the United States of Thracia claimed,

19:34.631 --> 19:35.924
were nowhere to be seen.

19:36.008 --> 19:40.387
On what basis did the United States
of Thracia make such a claim?

19:41.305 --> 19:42.848
There was this genius.

19:43.640 --> 19:44.558
A genius?

19:44.641 --> 19:49.396
It was believed that the Kingdom
of Persia's advanced robot army

19:49.479 --> 19:52.649
came from the mind of a genius scientist.

19:53.150 --> 19:55.235
What is the name of this scientist?

19:55.986 --> 19:58.197
He was commonly known as "Dr. Goji."

20:00.741 --> 20:02.826
No one knew his real name

20:02.910 --> 20:04.578
or what he looked like.

20:05.078 --> 20:10.167
We didn't even know
if such a person actually existed.

20:10.751 --> 20:14.129
That's about all we found out.

20:15.964 --> 20:19.426
But there was this one place
that we visited.

20:20.636 --> 20:23.263
<i>It was deep underground,
beneath an old mosque.</i>

20:24.932 --> 20:27.309
<i>I still don't know what to make
of what we saw there,</i>

20:27.809 --> 20:31.146
<i>those piles and piles of robot corpses.</i>

20:33.232 --> 20:35.442
The Kingdom explained to us

20:35.525 --> 20:40.364
that it was a dump for unusable robots.

20:43.825 --> 20:44.743
And then,

20:45.369 --> 20:47.120
the war started.

21:25.409 --> 21:27.035
You all right, Mont Blanc?

21:49.182 --> 21:50.934
You two hurt anywhere?

21:55.188 --> 21:58.817
Brando destroyed 2,895.

22:01.611 --> 22:03.739
I destroyed 2,962.

22:04.239 --> 22:06.992
How many did you destroy, Mont Blanc?

22:08.327 --> 22:09.453
A lot.

22:10.162 --> 22:11.413
A lot, huh?

22:12.873 --> 22:13.957
How impressive.

22:14.041 --> 22:15.667
It was 3,022.

22:21.089 --> 22:23.467
What are we doing here?

22:25.677 --> 22:28.805
We came here for a just cause, didn't we?

22:29.348 --> 22:32.434
To liberate robots from oppression.

22:32.517 --> 22:34.019
That's why we came, right?

22:39.858 --> 22:40.817
We...

22:44.029 --> 22:45.405
Access the network.

22:48.283 --> 22:52.120
<i>The palace of Darius XIV is about to fall.</i>

22:53.580 --> 22:57.209
<i>The peacekeeping forces
have entered the center of town.</i>

23:00.253 --> 23:01.922
<i>An "Emissary of Peace," huh?</i>

23:02.714 --> 23:04.299
Atom's got it easy.

23:06.885 --> 23:09.304
Why did we come here, you ask?

23:09.388 --> 23:11.890
Who is it that we should have destroyed?

23:14.935 --> 23:17.562
Who is it that we were supposed to hate?

23:18.772 --> 23:19.773
"Hate"?

23:20.357 --> 23:21.274
Yeah.

23:21.358 --> 23:24.736
What the heck is this thing
they call "hatred"?

24:02.858 --> 24:04.985
Brando!

24:05.068 --> 24:06.695
<i>What a landslide!</i>

24:06.778 --> 24:08.530
<i>Truly unbeatable!</i>

24:08.613 --> 24:13.493
<i>The final round of the ESKKKR Tournament
ended with his instant victory!</i>

24:13.577 --> 24:15.704
<i>Undefeated in 936 consecutive matches!</i>

24:15.787 --> 24:19.249
<i>Will we ever see an end
to the legend of this invincible hero?</i>

24:19.332 --> 24:21.668
<i>The strongest warrior in history!</i>

24:22.169 --> 24:24.671
<i>Brando!</i>

24:31.470 --> 24:34.139
That was an impressive match, Brando.

24:34.681 --> 24:37.976
Nah, I'm definitely
getting rickety these days.

24:38.518 --> 24:42.272
Sometimes, I can't even move
after a match, like right now.

24:45.692 --> 24:47.110
It's strange though.

24:47.861 --> 24:51.031
You all wear
the same pankration suits in the ring,

24:51.114 --> 24:53.492
but when you wear it,
you're the strongest.

24:54.034 --> 24:58.079
Experience is all you need
to win most matches.

24:58.580 --> 24:59.915
The rest is luck.

25:00.832 --> 25:01.875
Luck?

25:01.958 --> 25:06.838
Yeah. I know humans laugh
when a robot talks about luck.

25:07.756 --> 25:10.133
But I'm a lucky man.

25:21.520 --> 25:22.729
It's an old town, right?

25:23.522 --> 25:24.356
Yes.

25:30.362 --> 25:32.030
My place is upstairs.

25:40.163 --> 25:42.624
Your face says,

25:42.707 --> 25:46.753
"Why does a combat-sports superstar live
in a dump like this?"

25:46.836 --> 25:48.338
Not at all.

25:48.421 --> 25:53.677
Sure, with my fight money,
I could afford to live in a fancy mansion.

25:55.804 --> 25:56.638
However,

25:57.222 --> 25:59.891
I've chosen to use my money
on something else.

26:02.435 --> 26:05.230
I'm home!
King of the fighting world has returned!

26:05.313 --> 26:06.565
Daddy!

26:07.482 --> 26:08.858
Daddy!

26:08.942 --> 26:10.569
- You're home!
- Welcome back!

26:13.405 --> 26:14.531
All right, kiddos.

26:15.323 --> 26:16.950
Have you been good?

26:17.033 --> 26:18.827
Daddy, you're so strong!

26:18.910 --> 26:21.037
- You were amazing!
- You betcha!

26:21.830 --> 26:23.582
Welcome home, dear.

26:23.665 --> 26:24.499
Oh?

26:24.583 --> 26:27.419
I almost forgot. This is my wife, Mine.

26:28.044 --> 26:31.423
Pleased to meet you.
I'm Gesicht, of Europol.

26:32.007 --> 26:34.467
Time for dinner, everyone!

26:34.551 --> 26:36.386
- I'm starving!
- I'm so hungry!

26:36.469 --> 26:37.762
Let's go!

26:38.388 --> 26:40.515
Please come in.

26:43.184 --> 26:44.728
Catch me if you can!

26:44.811 --> 26:46.771
Hey! Don't go spilling things.

26:46.855 --> 26:48.231
Hey, you!

26:48.315 --> 26:50.817
No running during meals!

26:52.277 --> 26:54.070
Hey, mister, are you really a detective?

26:54.154 --> 26:54.988
I am.

26:55.780 --> 26:58.950
Then do you have a cool weapon
or something?

26:59.034 --> 27:01.953
No, I'm afraid I don't have anything cool.

27:02.537 --> 27:04.664
Stop with the silly questions!

27:04.748 --> 27:07.167
Keep that up, and you'll get a spanking!

27:11.504 --> 27:13.465
Please excuse them.

27:13.548 --> 27:16.384
No, I haven't had
such a fun meal in a while.

27:19.220 --> 27:22.891
What do you think?
A human-style meal isn't so bad, is it?

27:23.600 --> 27:25.644
Yes, so merry and lively.

27:26.936 --> 27:29.272
This is how it is in our house.

27:29.356 --> 27:31.483
Every day is a zoo event!

27:32.067 --> 27:35.028
Honey! Eat your salad!

27:35.570 --> 27:36.821
Oh...

27:36.905 --> 27:39.157
My mom is the strongest in this house!

27:39.949 --> 27:42.577
She's the world champion, right?

27:42.661 --> 27:46.581
Champion!

27:46.665 --> 27:49.084
Stop being silly and finish your dinner!

27:49.167 --> 27:52.379
Yikes! So scary!
She really is the champion!

28:02.347 --> 28:03.431
Is everyone asleep?

28:03.515 --> 28:04.349
Yeah.

28:09.729 --> 28:11.606
Don't drink too much.

28:17.278 --> 28:22.033
This is the life I've made for myself
with the fight money I've earned.

28:22.534 --> 28:23.451
Right.

28:24.619 --> 28:26.579
Because I fight for a living,

28:27.080 --> 28:31.835
Mine never knows when I'm going
to come home in pieces.

28:32.377 --> 28:37.424
For a while, she had to stay home alone,
worrying about me every day.

28:38.550 --> 28:41.344
That's when that policy came into effect.

28:42.470 --> 28:44.806
The Robot Adoption System.

28:44.889 --> 28:47.183
Right. We took in one first.

28:47.267 --> 28:50.353
And then a second
because the more, the merrier.

28:50.437 --> 28:52.063
Now we have five.

28:56.109 --> 28:57.736
It's a funny thing.

28:57.819 --> 29:02.282
Before kids, I never gave a shit
if I'd be torn into pieces in a match.

29:03.324 --> 29:04.284
But now,

29:04.951 --> 29:07.912
I want to live as long as possible.

29:08.496 --> 29:09.539
Weird, huh?

29:10.039 --> 29:13.460
I got kids, so I could die at any time.

29:13.543 --> 29:16.296
But now that I have them,
I don't want to die.

29:22.051 --> 29:24.053
I'm sure Mont Blanc wanted to live too.

29:27.348 --> 29:31.936
I met him
during the 39th Central Asian War.

29:32.729 --> 29:34.773
But more than the memory
of fighting together,

29:34.856 --> 29:37.817
I remember the fun times we had
doing silly things and talking all night.

29:38.318 --> 29:42.906
He told me about trees,
birds, all kinds of things.

29:43.698 --> 29:45.283
For a great guy like him

29:45.950 --> 29:47.786
to die the way he did...

29:56.252 --> 29:59.088
Do you know a robot named North No.2?

30:00.089 --> 30:01.800
Yeah, only by name.

30:03.176 --> 30:04.427
He's dead.

30:07.388 --> 30:08.723
Last week.

30:09.307 --> 30:14.646
He was living peacefully as the butler
of a composer in Scotland, and then...

30:15.980 --> 30:17.357
Was he killed?

30:18.358 --> 30:22.320
Yes. And now you're in danger too.

30:23.154 --> 30:25.240
You don't need to worry about me.

30:25.323 --> 30:27.075
I'm the king of the fighting world.

30:27.992 --> 30:29.744
That's why you're being targeted.

30:30.411 --> 30:31.788
I say bring it on.

30:32.372 --> 30:35.124
After what they did to Mont Blanc,

30:36.334 --> 30:38.670
I'll rip them apart, just you watch.

30:38.753 --> 30:42.799
Please don't be stupid!
If anything happens, call me right away!

30:43.716 --> 30:45.176
Would you like another?

30:45.760 --> 30:50.640
Oh, actually, this Turkish energy drink
is pretty potent.

30:51.266 --> 30:53.601
I'm ready for another.

30:53.685 --> 30:55.061
None for you.

30:57.814 --> 30:59.607
Fine.

31:00.608 --> 31:03.069
You sure you don't want me
to drive you back?

31:03.736 --> 31:06.239
Yes, I can grab a cab there.

31:06.781 --> 31:09.617
Okay. Come visit again soon.

31:10.451 --> 31:13.538
Thank you. I had a great time today.

31:14.664 --> 31:17.083
Yeah, kids are great, you know?

31:17.584 --> 31:19.544
You might want to give it a thought.

31:20.295 --> 31:24.007
Five of them like us
might be a bit much though.

31:25.800 --> 31:26.885
You're right.

31:28.303 --> 31:31.014
You can have the whole body for 500 ZEUS.

31:32.849 --> 31:33.933
What's the matter?

31:36.060 --> 31:39.522
Oh, it's nothing.
Maybe I had too much to drink.

31:39.606 --> 31:42.400
Are you sure you can get home by yourself?

31:44.569 --> 31:45.862
Yes, I'll be fine.

31:47.405 --> 31:48.823
All right, if you say so.

31:49.574 --> 31:52.285
Do take care of yourself.

31:52.368 --> 31:55.288
If anything happens, contact me.

31:57.624 --> 31:59.000
- Say...
- Hmm?

31:59.584 --> 32:02.962
I told you that winning
was up to one's luck, right?

32:05.423 --> 32:08.593
Humans leave things up to chance,

32:09.218 --> 32:10.929
but I say luck is something you take.

32:13.473 --> 32:16.726
It's because I have a family
that I've got luck on my side now.

32:16.809 --> 32:20.313
If anything happens, you just call me.

32:21.147 --> 32:23.608
I'm a lucky man.

32:26.069 --> 32:27.028
Yes.

32:27.111 --> 32:28.529
Thanks. I'm counting on you.

32:37.997 --> 32:39.040
<i>Please...</i>

32:41.250 --> 32:42.669
<i>Don't you die on me.</i>

33:06.359 --> 33:10.989
<i>Whoa! It's a double wrist lock!
Is this the end?</i>

33:11.072 --> 33:13.241
Rip his arm out!

33:16.244 --> 33:17.620
Break it!

33:17.704 --> 33:19.122
Twist it off!

33:24.919 --> 33:27.088
<i>There he is, the undefeated champion!</i>

33:27.171 --> 33:30.633
<i>What a perfect match
to defend the title of world champion!</i>

33:33.094 --> 33:38.224
<i>Everyone is intoxicated by the artistry
of Hercules, our god of battle!</i>

33:38.975 --> 33:40.893
Hercules!

33:40.977 --> 33:43.688
<i>Next month,
Hercules will finally have a showdown</i>

33:43.771 --> 33:47.316
<i>with Brando from Turkey,
the European champion!</i>

33:48.901 --> 33:51.988
<i>There it is, his signature pose!
The god of battle!</i>

33:54.949 --> 33:57.952
It's an amazing monument, Hercules.

33:59.996 --> 34:01.664
I told them not to.

34:02.582 --> 34:06.878
I said it would only ruin the view
of the world heritage site.

34:06.961 --> 34:11.132
But they ended up building a statue
of my pankration suit.

34:12.842 --> 34:15.344
Humans like that kind of stuff.

34:16.429 --> 34:18.681
I saw the match last night.

34:19.223 --> 34:21.059
You were strong, as usual.

34:22.685 --> 34:24.062
As usual, huh?

34:25.188 --> 34:28.733
Would you like to sit down
for a cup of tea and talk?

34:29.233 --> 34:30.985
I don't imitate humans.

34:32.570 --> 34:33.821
I'm a robot.

34:34.489 --> 34:37.533
A killing machine
that destroys his opponents.

34:38.534 --> 34:41.287
But in your recent matches...

34:42.997 --> 34:45.041
You think I've gone soft, right?

34:45.625 --> 34:48.002
That I held back last night
when it really mattered.

34:48.628 --> 34:52.131
Are you worried
about my next match with Brando?

34:54.175 --> 34:57.053
I heard you went to see him.

34:58.012 --> 34:58.930
Yes.

34:59.013 --> 35:00.306
He was in top shape.

35:00.389 --> 35:01.557
I'll bet.

35:02.058 --> 35:05.311
I've fought him many times,
and I know he's tough.

35:07.647 --> 35:09.273
Just like he was back then.

35:10.817 --> 35:15.029
During the 39th Central Asian War,
you mean?

35:22.829 --> 35:24.122
Detective Gesicht,

35:24.664 --> 35:28.417
do you know why humans
love building these monuments?

35:32.463 --> 35:34.298
Because they forget.

35:35.258 --> 35:40.847
Before their memory fades,
they build these things to remember.

35:40.930 --> 35:43.307
But look at us.

35:44.100 --> 35:48.896
Unless we erase them,
our memories will last forever.

35:49.522 --> 35:51.816
We remember things vividly.

35:53.234 --> 35:54.485
Our comrades in arms.

35:54.986 --> 35:58.364
Mountains of robot corpses on both sides.
Ours and theirs.

36:01.909 --> 36:03.411
That's how I learned

36:04.453 --> 36:05.621
about murderous intent.

36:08.583 --> 36:12.879
Ever since then, I haven't been able
to destroy my opponents.

36:14.589 --> 36:16.841
What do humans call this feeling?

36:18.843 --> 36:20.595
Compassion, perhaps?

36:24.056 --> 36:24.932
Say...

36:25.558 --> 36:26.392
Yes?

36:26.475 --> 36:27.602
Don't you think

36:29.020 --> 36:31.355
that we are evolving?

37:07.391 --> 37:08.559
<i>But why, Daddy?</i>

37:10.895 --> 37:14.065
You promised
that you'd come to the zoo with us!

37:14.649 --> 37:15.775
Yeah.

37:15.858 --> 37:17.443
Sorry, kiddos.

37:17.526 --> 37:21.280
Some work came up
that I have to attend to.

37:21.364 --> 37:22.740
What?

37:22.823 --> 37:25.243
You're just going to cancel on us?

37:25.326 --> 37:27.036
I'll come with you next time.

37:27.119 --> 37:28.621
It's a promise!

37:29.121 --> 37:31.332
You'll just break your promise again!

37:32.917 --> 37:35.253
No, I promise this as a man.

37:35.336 --> 37:39.966
And real men never break their promises.

37:40.841 --> 37:43.970
All right. Stop complaining!

37:44.595 --> 37:46.097
I'm coming with you.

37:46.681 --> 37:48.724
You're a liar, Daddy!

37:49.684 --> 37:51.060
I'm sorry.

37:52.103 --> 37:54.522
A sudden work matter...
Did something happen?

37:55.940 --> 37:58.484
Oh, it's an interview.

37:58.567 --> 38:00.027
An interview?

38:02.780 --> 38:05.908
It's a conversation with Miss Istanbul.

38:09.203 --> 38:13.874
I owe this editor I know,
and I couldn't say no.

38:15.209 --> 38:17.503
Well, have fun at this "interview."

38:18.254 --> 38:21.048
Hey, your husband
is the European champ now.

38:21.132 --> 38:23.759
I've got obligations...

38:40.484 --> 38:41.610
What's the matter?

38:42.528 --> 38:44.530
<i>Don't "what's the matter" me.</i>

38:44.613 --> 38:47.491
<i>You took your pankration suit out
without permission.</i>

38:47.575 --> 38:50.578
It won't be a problem.
I'll return it right away.

38:50.661 --> 38:52.872
<i>That's not the point.</i>

38:52.955 --> 38:55.333
<i>You even took the cargo truck
without asking.</i>

38:55.416 --> 38:58.836
<i>If anything happens,
they won't let you fight in the match.</i>

38:58.919 --> 39:01.922
<i>The match with Hercules
is coming up next--</i>

39:02.006 --> 39:03.299
That's exactly why.

39:03.382 --> 39:04.342
<i>Huh?</i>

39:05.134 --> 39:08.763
I'm borrowing it
to get ready for the next match.

39:08.846 --> 39:10.723
<i>That may be, but--</i>

39:17.772 --> 39:19.190
Relax, pal.

39:35.414 --> 39:39.794
Professor, do you think these incidents
were caused by a human, or...

39:39.877 --> 39:41.629
A robot?

39:42.421 --> 39:45.216
Or a combination of the two?

39:46.008 --> 39:51.889
The only precedent of a robot killing
a human is the case of Brau1589.

39:53.599 --> 39:54.809
Is that really true?

39:56.268 --> 39:57.269
Why do you ask?

39:57.937 --> 40:04.777
Never mind. So what kind of defects
did the AI of Brau1589 have?

40:06.237 --> 40:07.655
There weren't any.

40:08.239 --> 40:09.156
What?

40:09.990 --> 40:12.660
His AI was perfect.

40:13.327 --> 40:14.495
Perfect...

40:15.287 --> 40:17.331
A perfect AI killed a human...

40:17.998 --> 40:19.708
What does that mean?

40:21.210 --> 40:22.169
Could it be

40:23.462 --> 40:25.089
that it was human?

40:35.933 --> 40:37.935
This should be a good spot.

41:56.805 --> 41:57.890
What's the matter?

41:57.973 --> 41:59.141
Detective Gesicht?

42:00.184 --> 42:02.102
Patch yourself in, Hercules!

42:04.522 --> 42:05.564
No way!

42:07.066 --> 42:09.068
Atom, you patch in too!

42:14.949 --> 42:16.283
Atom, what's wrong?

42:17.201 --> 42:20.120
I'm getting a signal from Istanbul...

42:32.925 --> 42:35.135
Gesicht, what's going on here?

42:36.387 --> 42:38.305
It's communication from Brando.

42:41.433 --> 42:45.062
<i>Keep the channel... open!</i>

42:47.356 --> 42:48.274
Brando!

42:48.357 --> 42:49.483
Brando!

42:50.693 --> 42:54.363
<i>I'll show you the fight I have in me!</i>

42:54.863 --> 42:56.949
Stop! Stop it, Brando!

42:57.032 --> 42:59.201
Brando, run!

42:59.285 --> 43:02.288
I've identified his location.
He's on the coast of the Black Sea.

43:02.371 --> 43:03.706
Let's go, Gesicht!

43:07.668 --> 43:09.336
<i>To avenge...</i>

43:11.046 --> 43:12.715
<i>Mont Blanc!</i>

43:13.632 --> 43:17.261
Brando, do not take it head-on!
We're on our way!

43:35.237 --> 43:36.739
The signal is disturbed.

43:38.949 --> 43:40.284
What's happening, Atom?

43:41.827 --> 43:43.912
Professor, I have to go!

43:43.996 --> 43:45.789
But go where?

43:46.582 --> 43:48.876
Someone is attacking Brando.

43:49.585 --> 43:50.628
I have to hurry!

43:54.006 --> 43:55.341
<i>So strong...</i>

43:55.424 --> 43:57.176
<i>What the heck is this thing?</i>

44:17.488 --> 44:18.781
What was that?

44:20.532 --> 44:22.743
Brando, come in!

44:23.410 --> 44:24.453
Brando!

44:25.371 --> 44:26.205
Brando!

44:36.215 --> 44:37.132
The sea...

44:50.312 --> 44:51.522
<i>I did it.</i>

44:54.233 --> 44:55.192
Brando!

44:55.901 --> 44:57.111
<i>I beat it.</i>

44:58.737 --> 44:59.613
Brando!

45:00.698 --> 45:02.950
<i>I won.</i>

45:03.784 --> 45:07.705
<i>But it got me too.</i>

45:08.956 --> 45:10.874
We're coming! Hold on, Brando!

45:11.875 --> 45:13.043
<i>Hercules.</i>

45:15.003 --> 45:16.422
<i>Our next match,</i>

45:17.506 --> 45:19.550
<i>I was looking forward to it.</i>

45:20.968 --> 45:21.927
Me too.

45:22.428 --> 45:25.639
<i>I would have beat you.</i>

45:25.723 --> 45:26.974
Don't be silly!

45:27.933 --> 45:29.643
You never know!

45:32.688 --> 45:34.273
We're coming to get you!

45:35.232 --> 45:37.234
Just stay there and wait for us!

45:38.736 --> 45:45.367
<i>I'm sending you the data I analyzed
on the guy I just fought.</i>

45:46.118 --> 45:48.287
Brando, don't push yourself.

46:09.099 --> 46:10.100
<i>Huh?</i>

46:10.893 --> 46:12.519
<i>That's weird...</i>

46:13.187 --> 46:15.522
That's Brando's family.

46:17.941 --> 46:18.859
<i>Damn it...</i>

46:19.943 --> 46:20.986
<i>My circuits are</i>

46:21.779 --> 46:23.322
<i>all messed up.</i>

46:23.864 --> 46:25.824
Brando, that's enough.

46:26.909 --> 46:28.076
<i>Damn it.</i>

46:30.120 --> 46:31.830
<i>I can't transmit</i>

46:33.207 --> 46:34.208
<i>the correct data.</i>

46:35.167 --> 46:36.335
You've done enough.

46:37.544 --> 46:39.087
<i>That's odd.</i>

46:40.631 --> 46:41.757
<i>Sorry, guys.</i>

46:43.050 --> 46:45.719
<i>I can't control it.</i>

47:03.320 --> 47:04.822
<i>Detective Gesicht.</i>

47:06.824 --> 47:08.158
<i>Didn't I tell you?</i>

47:08.784 --> 47:11.203
<i>I'm a lucky man.</i>

47:12.037 --> 47:12.871
Yeah.

47:13.372 --> 47:14.540
<i>I promised my kids</i>

47:15.249 --> 47:17.668
<i>that I'd take them to the zoo.</i>

47:19.253 --> 47:22.381
<i>I made the promise as a man.</i>

47:26.218 --> 47:27.886
<i>Tell them</i>

47:29.388 --> 47:30.556
<i>not to worry.</i>

47:32.140 --> 47:34.810
<i>I'm a lucky man.</i>

47:40.232 --> 47:41.191
Brando!

47:48.156 --> 47:50.784
This is where Brando
sent his last transmission from.

47:51.285 --> 47:54.705
I've been sending him a signal,
but there's no response.

47:55.455 --> 47:56.498
All I can see is

47:57.165 --> 47:59.001
spilled oil on the water's surface

48:00.085 --> 48:03.463
and a huge amount of wreckage
at the bottom of the ocean.

48:05.883 --> 48:06.967
<i>Gesicht.</i>

48:07.050 --> 48:08.093
<i>Hercules.</i>

48:11.763 --> 48:13.140
For a brief moment,

48:13.223 --> 48:16.059
did you notice something mixed in
with the signals Brando sent?

48:16.143 --> 48:17.769
No, I didn't.

48:18.562 --> 48:22.566
Was it a signal from someone
other than Brando?

48:22.649 --> 48:28.530
Yes, a different AI
that had gone out of control.

48:29.239 --> 48:30.365
Something like noise.

48:31.366 --> 48:32.242
Noise?

48:33.493 --> 48:35.078
What could it be?

48:36.288 --> 48:39.207
- Atom, can you bring it up on the monitor?
- I can.

48:39.291 --> 48:41.960
<i>Atom, send it to us as well.</i>

48:42.502 --> 48:43.378
Understood.

48:44.504 --> 48:46.423
Here, right after this.

48:48.383 --> 48:50.928
What in the world is this?

49:01.104 --> 49:04.316
What do humans call this?

49:06.026 --> 49:07.402
Death incarnate.

49:08.278 --> 49:09.237
Death incarnate?

49:11.114 --> 49:12.240
Emotion.

49:17.245 --> 49:20.791
Overwhelming... pain.

49:34.096 --> 49:37.099
<i>This is the Blue Mosque Coliseum
in Istanbul.</i>

49:38.892 --> 49:43.230
<i>Scores of people are here
to mourn the death of their hero, Brando.</i>

49:50.195 --> 49:51.697
Daddy!

49:52.739 --> 49:56.910
We'll go now to our reporter on the scene.

49:58.620 --> 50:00.080
I'm here at the scene.

50:00.163 --> 50:03.834
The ocean floor around here
is covered with wreckage,

50:03.917 --> 50:07.129
and it is assumed
that most of it belongs to Brando.

50:08.505 --> 50:11.800
The police and the military
are continuing their search,

50:12.634 --> 50:15.137
but sources say it would be impossible

50:15.220 --> 50:18.640
to recover all the wreckage
due to the muddy ocean floor.

50:30.777 --> 50:33.905
How long are you going to let this go on?

50:33.989 --> 50:37.200
The deadline for defending your title
is coming soon!

50:38.285 --> 50:40.662
Are you listening to me, Hercules?

50:43.707 --> 50:48.587
If you're not going to fight,
then I'll sue you for breach of contract!

50:48.670 --> 50:52.674
I'm Al Haft, the biggest promoter
there is! You hear me?

50:59.014 --> 51:00.932
They haven't found a damn thing.

51:02.517 --> 51:04.895
They haven't found
a single piece of the killer.

51:06.063 --> 51:09.858
All they've found so far
are pulverized pieces of Brando.

51:10.776 --> 51:13.779
Brando fought the killer here and won.

51:14.696 --> 51:17.824
So, why can't we
find pieces of the killer?

51:19.701 --> 51:20.619
Hercules.

51:21.369 --> 51:24.664
Even the military and the police have
given up on recovering everything.

51:25.165 --> 51:29.294
So, why should you be the one to do it,
let alone out of your own pocket?

51:31.588 --> 51:33.715
Is it your friendship with Brando?

51:34.633 --> 51:36.802
Your fans are all waiting for you.

51:36.885 --> 51:39.513
For Hercules, the god of battle,
to come back to the ring.

51:40.013 --> 51:41.807
I am too.

51:43.934 --> 51:45.519
So please, Hercules.

51:45.602 --> 51:46.603
Come back--

51:51.608 --> 51:55.278
Hercules! We found Brando's arms!

51:55.946 --> 51:56.863
Good work!

51:57.405 --> 51:59.241
Take great care with the recovery!

51:59.324 --> 52:01.743
Actually, it's a little complicated!

52:02.369 --> 52:05.163
They were found on a rock reef
about 100 km away from here,

52:05.247 --> 52:07.916
not on the ocean floor!

52:07.999 --> 52:08.959
We'll take you there!

52:10.293 --> 52:11.253
Wait!

52:12.254 --> 52:13.213
Hercules!

52:14.172 --> 52:17.509
Come back!
Come back and fight one more time!

52:20.679 --> 52:21.805
Hercules.

52:33.525 --> 52:35.861
Right over there, on that rock!

52:46.663 --> 52:48.039
What the...

53:06.308 --> 53:08.143
Brando's memory chip.

53:09.269 --> 53:10.103
Horns.

53:12.480 --> 53:14.357
I don't believe this...

53:15.483 --> 53:16.401
The killer

53:17.444 --> 53:18.904
isn't dead yet!

53:32.500 --> 53:37.005
Brando!

56:10.700 --> 56:14.412
Subtitle translation by: Astrid Oliver
